{
  "schemaVersion": "2",
  "name": "obid's browser: the person's ways out of a page state, Try again and Reload, Go back, and the page's own dialog answered Leave or Stay, each signed and only on a tab the signing device holds",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "BROWSER-26, board 10, ported from the lab's LAB-BROWSERAPI-8 (workflows/lab/browserapi/ways-out.json) onto obid (core/crates/obid/src/browser/routes.rs, way_out; api/state.rs, Api::way_out; driver/person_page.rs): the agent's navigate to a site that refuses fails and the tab is failed. POST …/reload unsigned is refused (unsigned), with the job's token too (bad_token: the agents' tools never get these routes); signed by a device on a tab nobody holds it is refused (not_held); once the device takes, another device is refused (not_holder); a reload while the site still refuses leaves the tab failed (browser); with the site fixed the same address loads and the tab is ready. Go back: the agent goes from the home page to the second, the device takes, …/back brings the home page back. The page's dialog: the agent clicks Leave, the page asks its confirm and the tab is in state dialog; the device takes, …/dialog {accept: false} is Stay (the page is still there, the dialog gone), with no dialog left a second answer is refused (no_dialog), and once the page asks again {accept: true} is Leave (the page goes home). The lab's own read of the tab's URL (lab.browser.read) is the agent's snapshot here, which reads the live URL too. A scratch obid on the stand-ins, a Codex job sleeping as its agent with its broker token, the lab API's fixture sites, the real agent-browser and Chrome for Testing obid installs.",
  "trigger": {
    "http": {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/browser/tabs/{id}/reload"
    }
  },
  "steps": [
